---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const root='/equipment/12-07/';
const spec='https://asset-downloads.zeiss.com/catalogs/download/mic/6e5f43dd-cfd4-4822-a511-3ebdaf7859bd/EN_product-info_Lightsheet-7_rel1-0.pdf#page=21';
const photo='https://www.zeiss.com/content/dam/rms/reference-master/resource-center/insights-hub/insights-hub-france/life-sciences/ls7.png/_jcr_content/renditions/original.image_file.1920.1920.file/ls7.png';
const institution='https://www.uab.edu/cores/ircp/hrif-equipment/fluorescence-microscopes/zeiss-lightsheet-7';
---
<Layout pageTitle="ZEISS Lightsheet 7 and inert plane replay" subtitle="" wide={true}>
 <main class="equipment-page ls">
  <p><a href="/simulations/equipment/#equipment-12-07">↩ Equipment register · 12-07</a></p>
  <h1>ZEISS Lightsheet 7 · plane replay</h1>
  <p>Explore the <strong>closed, unpowered Lightsheet 7</strong> main module, not the Lattice model. Play through an artificial geometric volume on a separate virtual display. It is an offline image viewer, not an acquisition or optical simulation.</p>
  <div class="ls-cols">
   <section aria-label="3D exterior">
    <div class="ls-buttons"><button id="ls-front" type="button">Reset orbit</button><button id="ls-rear" type="button">Rear enclosure</button><button id="ls-display" type="button">Replay panel close-up</button></div>
    <div id="ls-view" role="img" aria-label="Interactive exterior of dormant ZEISS Lightsheet 7 beside a separate synthetic display"></div>
    <p id="ls-model">Loading metric model…</p>
   </section>
   <section class="ls-read">
    <h2>Inert fiducial volume</h2>
    <canvas id="ls-plane-canvas" width="640" height="400" role="img" aria-label="XY voxel plane with labeled synthetic fiducial patches and a 160 micrometer scale bar"></canvas>
    <label for="ls-plane">Z plane index</label><input id="ls-plane" type="range" min="0" max="20" step="1" value="10"/>
    <div class="ls-buttons"><button id="ls-prev" type="button">Previous plane</button><button id="ls-next" type="button">Next plane</button><button id="ls-reset" type="button">Reset replay</button><button id="ls-save" type="button">Export plane JSON</button></div>
    <p id="ls-status" role="status"></p><p id="ls-scale"></p>
   </section>
  </div>
  <section id="ls-refs">
   <h2>Reference sheet</h2>
   <p><a href={photo}>ZEISS front-view photograph</a>: raised lid, off-center crown, closed fascia seams, dark plinth and model ID. Compare with “Reset orbit” in the original rendering above. The side camera blocks visible in the photograph are optional and outside this model. <a href={institution}>UAB installed-system photograph</a>: confirms the standalone main module as distinct from worktables and displays. These photos are linked rather than republished. Rear vents and split-panel geometry in the interactive render are estimates.</p>
   <figure><img src={root+'front-reference.webp'} alt="Original simulation: pearl enclosure, shallow plinth and a physically separate replay display" width="513" height="332" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Original browser-rendered model, front three-quarter view. The raised crown and plinth are part of the dormant module; the separate visible screen is our synthetic viewer.</figcaption></figure>
   <div class="ls-table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Reference specifications" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th>Specification</th><th>Value</th><th>Source / effect</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td>Unpacked closed main module</td><td>800 mm width × 450 mm depth × 500 mm height, nominal</td><td><a href={spec}>ZEISS Product Info, English, technical specifications p. 21</a>; GLB envelope</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Unpacked nominal mass</td><td>75 kg</td><td>Same source, documentation only. No dynamics or load bearing modeled.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Synthetic volume sample count and pitch</td><td>64 × 40 × 21; 8 × 8 × 20 µm</td><td>Author-defined geometric exercise, not optical performance or ZEISS acquisition settings.</td></tr>
   </tbody></table></div>
  </section>
  <section id="ls-proof">
   <h2>Scale and verification</h2>
   <p>Inputs are the built-in inert volume and an integer plane index 0–20. A voxel center on axis i is (index + ½) × spacing. Each sphere has a 24 µm radius; marked pixels have centers at most 24 µm from a sphere center. Output is row-major class labels (0 = background, 1–3 = fiducials) from the bottom row, in-plane scale and surveyed center metadata. No measured optical images, acquisition, registration, tissue or preparation are included. The original two-view acceptance is not implemented.</p>
   <div class="ls-table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Verification results" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Tolerance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
   <tr><td>Plane index 10</td><td>210 µm from sample corner; 29 pixels per F1 / F2</td><td>210 µm; 29 / 29 pixels</td><td>Exact grid</td></tr>
   <tr><td>Next plane</td><td>230 µm; F1 / F2 patches shrink to 9 pixels each</td><td>230 µm; 9 / 9 pixels</td><td>Exact grid</td></tr>
   <tr><td>Scale bar and markers</td><td>20 px = 160 µm; 24 px center distance = 192 µm</td><td>160 µm and 192 µm</td><td>Exact integer arithmetic</td></tr>
   <tr><td>GLB cabinet envelope</td><td>800 × 500 × 450 mm (XYZ)</td><td>800 × 500 × 450 mm (XYZ)</td><td>0.05 mm from source nominal</td></tr>
   </tbody></table></div>
   <p><a href={root+'lightsheet7.glb'} download>Download metric GLB</a> · <a href={root+'build-model.py'} download>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={root+'example-plane.json'}>Example JSON</a> · <a href={root+'xr.json'}>XR action names and bounds</a> (headset not tested).</p>
  </section>
 </main>
 <script is:inline>window.lightReplay=import('/equipment/12-07/replay.mjs');</script>
 <script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/12-07/client.mjs';</script>
</Layout>
<style>
 .ls{max-width:82rem;margin:0 auto;padding-inline:1rem}.ls-cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.7fr) minmax(16rem,1fr);gap:1.5rem;align-items:start}.ls-buttons{display:flex;gap:.45rem;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:.55rem 0}.ls button{border:1px solid currentColor;background:transparent;color:inherit;padding:.42rem .62rem;border-radius:.18rem;font:inherit}.ls button:not(:disabled){cursor:pointer}.ls button:disabled{opacity:.45}#ls-view{height:clamp(16rem,36vw,36rem);background:#29383b;overflow:hidden;touch-action:none;border-radius:.2rem}#ls-view :global(canvas){display:block;width:100%;height:100%}#ls-plane-canvas{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:.2rem}.ls-read{border:1px solid currentColor;padding:.8rem 1rem;border-radius:.3rem}.ls-read label{display:block;margin-top:.6rem}.ls input{width:96%}.ls table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}.ls th,.ls td{border-bottom:1px solid currentColor;text-align:left;padding:.35rem .5rem}.ls section{margin-bottom:1.3rem}.ls figure{margin:1rem 0;max-width:33rem}.ls figure img{max-width:100%;height:auto}@media(max-width:730px){.ls-cols{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
 .ls-table-scroll{max-width:100%;overflow-x:auto}
</style>
